#
# Cursor names for the web viewer.
#
# The web client asks for pseudo-encoding -524289. Other clients do not.
# When the cursor's last row spells a name, a client that asked receives
# the image unchanged. Everyone else gets the picture with the row
# removed.
#
# The cursor drawn into the screen is the picture with the row removed.
# That drawing is used for a client with no local cursor, and when the
# pointer moves without a pointer event from the client.
#
